  "invariants": [
    "PC2.a and PC2.b each have three hydraulically separate water channels.",
    "Four S3 instances: two parallel tanks in climate supply and two parallel tanks in intermediate supply; each circuit's return bypasses its tanks.",
    "SC2 primary and secondary never share a hydraulic edge.",
    "SC1 primary water never shares a hydraulic edge with potable water.",
    "Groundwater is open between extraction and restitution. S4 vessels are side branches.",
    "Changing season changes heat transfer, not the nominal water-flow topology.",
    "No installed refrigerant piping is inferred from the water-side drawing.",
    "Domestic draw-off exits at TAP and COLD.tap boundaries; only the warm stairwell distribution recirculation branch (ACR/RCP, ~48 C) returns via P02/P03 toward the mixer and S2 inlet."
  ],
